WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:03.752
- [Narrator] Does
pineapple belong on pizza?

00:00:03.752 --> 00:00:04.585
- No!
- Yeah.

00:00:04.585 --> 00:00:05.418
- What?
- No way!

00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:06.540
- What on Earth?
- OK, stop!

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.060
Sweden sees your pineapple
and raises you ...

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:15.060
banana on pizza, curry on
pizza, and kebab on pizza.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.317
Seriously, Sweden?

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:20.900
(quirky music)

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.340
So, let's forget about pineapple,
because here in Sweden,

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.240
they have a completely
different take on pizza.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.540
Here, it's a pizza topping free for all.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.550
Mehmed has been cooking
pizzas for 25 years,

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.140
and he will tell you anything goes.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.291
Things like banana.

00:00:38.291 --> 00:00:41.208
(foreign language)

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.776
So, what do the Swedes eat in the summer?

00:00:49.776 --> 00:00:52.693
(foreign language)

00:01:05.752 --> 00:01:08.040
I mean, who doesn't love a kebab?

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.241
So, Özen of La Babca
pizzeria, what's on your menu?

00:01:11.241 --> 00:01:14.158
(foreign language)

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:15.903
Shrimp?

00:01:15.903 --> 00:01:18.210
Oh, say it ain't so, Sweden!

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.670
Oh, there's more.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:21.960
There's curry pizza, which is chicken,

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.150
banana, curry, and pineapple.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.600
Or my favorite, tropicana:
ham, banana, and béarnaise.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.023
Mm-mm.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:31.883
Wait.

00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:34.365
This isn't just a late night snack, is it?

00:01:34.365 --> 00:01:37.282
(foreign language)

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.870
Now for the real question.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.839
Why did Sweden reinvent
an already perfect food?

00:01:51.839 --> 00:01:54.756
(foreign language)

00:02:08.266 --> 00:02:11.847
And now the most
important part: the taste.

00:02:11.847 --> 00:02:12.680
Mm!

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.410
This is really good!

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.993
(upbeat music)

